==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}}, from {{term|πυλωρός||gatekeeper|tr=pulōros|lang=grc}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|pylori|pyloruses}}

# {{context|anatomy|lang=en}} The opening in a [[vertebrate]], including [[human]]s, at the lower end of the [[stomach]] that opens into the [[duodenum]].
# A [[muscular]] or [[myovascular]] structure that controls the opening of an orifice or [[lumen]] of an organ.

====Synonyms====
* [[pyloric sphincter]]

====Derived terms====
* [[pyloric]]

